      "case": "five authorial enclosure questions and separate footnote annotation",
      "requirement": "Keep the five actual authorial enclosure questions distinct from the body: origin and foreign name, habits, cage display versus freedom, sex/individual differences among pure birds, and breeding true in form/colour. The intermediary search and Holland fallback are in the cover body, not among those five questions. Preserve uncertain Kinder/Trinder identity without choosing a person; inspect segmented typography for supported rendering. Body asks about a plant-culture report, while editorial summary names Cnicus; do not import the summary title. Exclude the separate undated Darwin note quoted in footnote8. The authentic authorial enclosure is not an annotation.",
